Features supported by rustc for this target:
    alu32           - Enable ALU32 instructions.
    static-syscalls - Enable static syscalls.
    crt-static      - Enables C Run-time Libraries to be statically linked.

Code-generation features supported by LLVM for this target:
    callx-reg-src   - Encode Callx destination register in the src field.
    dummy           - unused feature.
    dwarfris        - Disable MCAsmInfo DwarfUsesRelocationsAcrossSections.
    dynamic-frames  - Enable dynamic frames.
    new-call-conv   - Enable new call convetion for SBFv2.
    no-lddw         - Disable the lddw instruction.
    no-neg          - Disable the neg instruction.
    pqr-instr       - Enable the PQR instruction class.
    reloc-abs64     - Fix 64bit data relocations.
    reverse-sub     - Reverse the operands in the 'sub reg, imm' instruction.
    solana          - Enable Solana extensions.

Use +feature to enable a feature, or -feature to disable it.
For example, rustc -C target-cpu=mycpu -C target-feature=+feature1,-feature2

Code-generation features cannot be used in cfg or #[target_feature],
and may be renamed or removed in a future version of LLVM or rustc.

